@startuml

start

:Power management subsystem architected as a set of concurrent RTOS tasks;
:Continuously monitor all power rails via PMIC and BMS;

if (Load > rated capacity?) then (yes)
  :Initialize multi-channel parallel processing routine;

  fork
    :Check main power rail state;
    if (Voltage fluctuations > defined threshold?) then (yes)
      :Enter iterative monitoring mode;
      repeat
        :Sample rail via timer-driven ADC within dedicated ISR;
      repeat while (Stability confirmed?) is (no)
    else (no)
    end if
  fork again
    :High-priority task managed by priority queue;
    :Execute backup power switching logic;
    :Acquire mutex;
    :Assess backup power state from BMS over CRC-protected CAN bus;
    if (Sufficient?) then (yes)
      :Command switch to backup rail;
    else (no)
      :Initialize generator power rail via FADEC;
    end if
    :Re-verify energy supply status;
    if (Stability restored?) then (yes)
      :Conclude process;
    else (no)
      :Continue iterative detection with exponential backoff algorithm;
    end if
  end fork

else (no)
end if

:Telemetry monitor task woken by periodic timer interrupts;
:Run in continuous loop;
:Log debounced events to ring buffer;
:Manage fault recovery via staged backoff and verification cycles;
:Hardware watchdog supervises entire process;

stop

@enduml
